  "pitfalls": [
    "CTR, CPC, CPM, CPL, CPA and ROAS are recomputed from summed spend, impressions, clicks, leads and conversions; the platforms' own ratio columns are never averaged across days or campaigns.",
    "Each ad platform takes credit for the same sale (attribution double counting), so conversions and revenue summed across channels usually exceed what the business actually booked.",
    "Reach and unique users are de-duplicated within each row and cannot be added across days or campaigns.",
    "Conversions arrive with a lag: the most recent days look weak until late conversions are attributed, so compare complete periods.",
    "ROI and ROAS here are on revenue, not profit: a ROAS above 1 can still lose money once product and delivery costs are counted.",
    "Small campaigns give noisy rates; a CTR or CPA from a few hundred impressions or a handful of conversions is not reliable."
